  "answer": "The folder-size part of this request has been filed before. PowerToys#356 is the main ticket, and the others (#38791, #7260) were closed as duplicates of it. It is still only a feature request, and PowerToys has no feature that shows folder sizes in File Explorer's Details view. Add your +1 or your use case to #356. Until it is built, third-party tools can do this: WinDirStat, WizTree, the Folder Size shell extension, the Files app, or Everything. PowerToys Peek also shows a folder's size when you preview a folder. The ticket's comments don't ask for the colour-coding by size or the custom folder colours. A separate request, #30512 (custom folder thumbnails and colours), covers the colour idea, but it is a different request."
